{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'continuation|ownership|lineariz|migration|capabil|portable|resume|park' docs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md docs/design/dao.stream.md\"","aggregated_output":"docs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md:25:realization is bounded evict-oldest, so internal rings in the current migration\ndocs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md:99:| Blocking on IO | Parked continuations registered as transport waiters; wake converts to run-queue entries | `yin/vm/engine.cljc` (`make-woken-run-queue-entries`) |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md:100:| Continuation shipping | Hand-built k-stream with per-VM cursors at the app layer | `datomworld/continuation_transport.cljc` |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md:108:`:wait-set`, `:parked`) are private vectors in one VM's state map, popped by\ndocs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md:119:addressed medium that executes. Control, environment, store, and continuation\ndocs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md:143:  synchronization, no park/resume, no waiters. Blocking — and the waiter\ndocs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md:145:- **Cursors double as pointers.** The continuation stack is an append-only\ndocs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md:151:- **Immutability is observable only at park points.** Hot logs may run on\ndocs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md:152:  transients and snapshot to the persistent view when the machine parks —\ndocs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md:167:store, and continuation are all logs, and `t` is the step counter with `as-of`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md:183:  of its fold; park/resume boundaries are the natural consistency points, and\ndocs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md:184:  the park machinery already exists.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md:212:   captured by a lambda body, no