{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"The canonical format does not inherently violate Axiom 2: a shared encoding still needs an interpreter to give it meaning. The main concerns are the migration guarantees—source mappings cannot reconstruct optimized state on their own, and the proposed payload omits dependencies that local resume takes from the existing VM. I’ll check the ownership and effect-ordering contracts next."}}
